Verse 1:
[F]I need Thee [C7]precious [Dm]Jesus,
For [Bb]I am [F]ver[Bb]y[C]poor;
[C7]A[F]stranger [C7]and a [F]pil[Gm]grim,
I [F]have no [C7]earthly [F]store.
I [Bb]need the [Bbm]love of [F]Jesus
To [Bb]cheer me [Bbm]on my [F]way,
To guide my [Bb]doubt[F]ing [Gm7]foot [C7]steps,
To [F]be my [C7]strength [F]and stay.

Verse 2:
[F]I need the [C7]heart of Jesus to [Dm]feel each anxious care,
[Bb]To tell [F]my every trial, [Bb]and all [C]my sorrows share.
[C7]I need [F]the Holy [C7]Spirit to [F]teach me [Gm]what I am,
[F]To show me more [C7]of Jesus, to point [F]me to the Lamb.

Verse 3:
[F]I need Thee [C7]precious Jesus, I hope [Dm]to see Thee soon,
[Bb]Encircled with [F]the rainbow, [Bb]and seated [C]on Thy throne.
[C7]There with [F]Thy blood-bought [C7]children, my [F]joy shall [Gm]ever be
[F]To sing Thy [C7]ceaseless praises, to gaze, [F]my Lord, on Thee.
